  "recommendations": [
    "condition: Add SUPPORTED claims that restate conditions correctly in new words, so 'condition mentioned' is not a contradiction cue.",
    "direct: Add CONTRADICTED and INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE claims that copy most of the evidence wording but change one decisive detail, so near-verbatim wording is not a perfect support cue.",
    "distractor_sentence: Distractors are INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE by construction; keep them, but report per-phenomenon accuracy so they cannot inflate the headline score.",
    "missing_information: Add INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE claims with high word overlap with the evidence (same topic, unstated detail), so low overlap is not the only signal for missing information.",
    "multi_sentence_partial: Partial-evidence examples are INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE by construction; add more multi-sentence claims so this group is not tiny.",
    "numerical: Add SUPPORTED claims that restate or correctly instantiate numbers ('a $3,000 purchase' under 'up to $5,000') and INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE claims with numbers the evidence never mentions, so 'number changed' is not a perfect contradiction cue.",
    "paraphrase: Add paraphrased claims that are CONTRADICTED or unsupported, not only supported ones.",
    "Text cue direct_quotation=True predicts SUPPORTED for 90% of 392 examples; add counter-examples with the same cue and a different label.",
    "Text cue scope_terms_not_in_evidence=True predicts INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE for 86% of 106 examples; add counter-examples with the same cue and a different label.",
    "Text cue content_overlap=<0.4 predicts INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE for 90% of 143 examples; add counter-examples with the same cue and a different label.",
    "Text cue content_overlap=>=0.95 predicts SUPPORTED for 90% of 392 examples; add counter-examples with the same cue and a different label.",
    "A rule using only surface cues (number mismatch, verbatim overlap, negation, overlap, format) beats the majority class on held-out splits. In M6.3, report this cue-only baseline next to every model and break results down by phenomenon; a model that merely matches it has learned shortcuts."
  ]
